    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Liu Yu, a general of the Jin who had retaken <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a>, received the abdication of Sima Dewen in 420 and founded the Song dynasty.</li><li>The Reign of Yuanjia (425–453) under Emperor Wen is remembered as one of the relative golden ages of the Southern Dynasties.</li><li>Failed wars against Northern Wei and murderous succession struggles weakened the dynasty until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiao-daocheng">Xiao Daocheng</a> took the throne as Emperor of Qi in 479.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The astronomer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zu-chongzhi">Zu Chongzhi</a>, who lived in the Liu Song period, is noted for calculating pi to seven decimal places.</p></aside>
    </section>

